+/* The guest address of the tail jump itself, for the failure message.
+ *
+ * A tail jump pushes no return address, so when its target turns out not to
+ * be code there is nothing on the stack to say where it came from -- the
+ * report named a float as its caller, because that is what happened to be on
+ * top. Nearly all of these are switch dispatches, and a switch that jumps to
+ * a non-address has read its jump table out of range, so the one thing worth
+ * knowing is which switch. The lifter knows that at emit time; this carries
+ * it through. */
+extern uint32_t g_itail_site;
+
